l nine exact-head CI contexts were green. Fresh elaboration of the current Claims source passed, with only the retained Claim 17-2 `sorry`. Axiom inspection of Claims 17-1/17-3, `exists_subLineWitness`, and `restricted_lines_consistency_bound` found only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\\\\n\\\\nThe universal constants remain outside all parameter quantifiers. The implemented Claims 17-1/17-3 bounds use `C = 2`; the Z proof uses the separate Z marginal and derives its deficit without Claim 17-2. No new proof holes, bypasses, or load-bearing hypotheses were found. Claim 17-2\\\\u2019s existing arbitrary-witness contract remains unresolved on this head; the separate repairs are not current proof content. The prose lane owns the distinct complex-scalar versus real-part comparison.\\\\n\\\\nThe external `lean-conventions` skill was unavailable; checked-in conventions were used. No files or workflow records were modified.\\\\n\\\\nNative review binding: 48c8adbc83d749b0b79fb9faac681534 37a2e268bc1ef7434e13c9b8b3daf3c02d18b94e 513a56fa3336424731bec2e678fa15c8bbf06f6bb83e4c4542edb1fba2c18b9e\\\\n\\\\n## Prose review\\\\n\\\\nF1: The blueprint defines scalar approximation by the absolute difference at lines 46\\\\u201347 and displays the expectations themselves in Claim 17-1. However, `Claims.lean:360` and `Claims.lean:375` take real parts before averaging. The ordered product of the two point projections need not be Hermitian, and no reality assertion accompanies this signature. A bound on the real part does not establish the displayed complex modulus bound. Prove the complex overlap estimate, or record the real-part result separately without certifying the paper statement.\\\\n\\\\nF2: The proof at blueprint lines 1604\\\\u20131609 uses \\\\\\\\(W^2\\\\\\\\), bounds its expectation by \\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\delta_Q\\\\\\\\), and concludes an error at most \\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_Q}\\\\\\\\). For \\\\\\\\(W=Q-M_ZM_X\\\\\\\\), the squared norm involves